From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:16:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(loop_accounting): close a raised lease pass as an error,
 clamp fork depth, survive ConfigBackendUnavailable, read interval outside the
 lock, fold tids at thread exit [daveey]

Follow-ups from the non-blocking points of the PR #2401 reviews (5894758704 @bfbbdfd221,
5895222011 @d58f1856db). Kanban card t_01a1d5edd93f87e8.

1. HostLoopLease span across a raising pass. kanban_annotation_host.loop skips beat() when
   _holder_pass() raises, so the next beat() recorded one lease.<name> run spanning two passes
   plus the sleep, errors=0. held() now closes a still-open span with errors+=1 before opening a
   new one on every true held(). (The errored run's wall still includes the sleep up to the next
   held(): the lease cannot see where the pass raised. Its CPU is the pass's.)
2. Fork while a nested pass is open. _after_fork_child clears the thread-local depth, so the
   two exits drove it to -1 and the thread never counted another outermost pass. Pass.__exit__
   clamps with max(0, ...); span_close and record() test depth <= 0.
3. _setting caught only Exception; ConfigBackendUnavailable is a SystemExit and escaped
   begin_process at boot. It is now caught by name (the config modules are imported first, so
   a missing module still falls back to the defaults).
4. start() called interval_s() -> load_config() while holding _lock, stalling every pass exit
   on every thread behind one config read. The interval is read before the lock.
5. Linux tid reuse. Each thread that accounts CPU holds a _ThreadExit in the threading.local;
   CPython drops it when the thread ends (synchronously, before join() returns and before the
   kernel can reuse the tid), and its __del__ queues the tid in a lock-free deque. The next
   holder of _lock folds queued tids into exited_accounted before adding CPU, so a thread given
   a reused tid starts at 0. The snapshot's live-set fold stays as the backstop.
6. Docstring named unaccounted_cpu_s; the key is process.unaccounted_live_cpu_s, None without
   procfs.

Proof (tests/hermes_cli/test_loop_accounting.py):
- RED on origin/main sources (tests only): 5 failed, 18 passed
  (raised-lease pass, fork depth, tid reuse [0.030 inherited], ConfigBackendUnavailable,
  interval read under lock).
- GREEN: test_loop_accounting + bench + test_host_loop_lease + test_kanban_remote_index +
  test_kanban_unloaded_host_lease + test_kanban_annotation_host: 111 passed.
- Bench (best of 5 x 50k passes, this worker): 3.0 us/pass (budget 20 us).
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok (1 pre-existing advisory HX012 on start()).
